WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:05.120
The first match of the Friendship Cup's 
second round was Yuzu versus Sergey.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:11.260
It's wrong to force a man 
on his last legs to duel.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.350
You're looking forward to seeing someone 
sent underground that much?

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.830
Yuzu wanted to use her duel to warn of 
the interdimensional war's danger.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.260
You...

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.740
You think you've already won?

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.080
Not that you're going to win... 
But that you already have?

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.010
That's what you seem to think.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.160
It isn't a face desperately trying to win,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.770
but a face already assured of victory...

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.760
That is most beautiful when crushed.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:47.320
Vandarlizuma attacks Bloom Prima!

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.200
An Action Card!

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.880
Your struggle is beautiful.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:00:59.800
But...

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.940
Unsightly!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:09.880
Yuzu!

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.340
Fool!

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.110
All available security to the place she landed.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:34.760
That's a surprise!

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.580
Sergey achieves an unbelievable 
come-from-behind victory!

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.710
While Yuzu Hiiragi appears to have 
been thrown from the duel lane,

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:45.050
crashing into a nearby building.

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:49.360
Smoke is rising from the building, 
and we can't see inside.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.130
We can't tell if Yuzu is safe or not!

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.700
Yuzu!

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.580
D-Wheels.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:03.770
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.480
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.920
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.110
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:50.010
Storm of Revolution

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.020
S-Sergey Volkov has come back!

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.880
Despite his injury, he's triumphantly returned, 
with a come-from-behind victory!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.410
I came... I came.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:15.770
Did you see that face contorted in terror?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.200
So beautiful!

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.460
Duelist Crusher...

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.640
Is that the way he crushed all those duelists?

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.610
Creepy.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:37.560
Reiji Akaba... You laughed, saying that 
Roget's plans were foolish.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:42.530
But his plan seems to be moving smoothly along.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.300
Is that acceptable?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.000
For you to watch from here, doing nothing...

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.580
Security is on the field!

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.980
They've captured Sergey!

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.560
They're taking him off the field.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:14.340
To lose himself to such a pitiful duel...

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.260
He will require some refurbishing.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.000
Forget that! Help Yuzu!

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.000
Is Yuzu okay?!

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:31.830
Yuzu... Leave the rest to me.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:35.350
I swear to pick up where you left off!

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.230
Open up! Open this door!

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.100
Time for the next match.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.430
Shinji Weber versus Yuya Sakaki!

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:48.960
Shinji versus Yuya?

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.630
I'll show you to the venue.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.470
Sam! Is Yuzu okay?

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.330
I don't know.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.840
You don't know?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.800
There's no point in asking him.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.700
Shinji!

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.760
No one cares what happens to losers.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:12.970
We're nothing but a show for those Tops.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.840
When a game piece is lost, it's gone.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.250
Gone?

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:21.460
No one's going to help her?!

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.500
Losers are abandoned.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:25.430
That's the way of this world now.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:31.350
Put another way, Yuzu is a 
sacrifice to that world...

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:36.340
That's the reason I'm fighting to 
change this rotten society!

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:44.560
To accomplish that, we, the oppressed 
Commons, must unite our energy

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.500
and overturn the Tops' control of this world!

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:51.020
This time, I will get the Commons to rise up.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:55.390
Sorry, Yuya, but I'll need to use 
you as a stepping stone!

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.920
This is no time for that!

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:01.270
Yuzu could be suffering at this very moment.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.600
She could be injured, waiting to be saved.

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:07.280
This is no time to be dueling!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.000
Use the duel to make your case!

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:12.580
Show that we have the power to change society.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:19.020
Make the Commons rise up, so we 
don't see any more Yuzus!

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.050
You're saying you don't care about 
Yuzu, who's suffering right now?!

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.150
I'm talking about what I can accomplish now.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:29.200
In our position, we cannot save Yuzu Hiiragi.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.850
So we have to use our duel to tell the spectators

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:35.030
to forge a new future and create a better world!

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.590
You want to say something, right?

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.800
Win the duel and say it to the spectators!

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.380
It's time for the second match of the 
Friendship Cup's second round.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.590
The duelists have arrived at the starting grid!

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.130
I'm going to make you rise up now.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:04.860
Wait for me, Yuzu... I'll be there soon!

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.330
She isn't there?

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:08.500
No, sir.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.970
We're expanding the search area 
to try and find her, but...

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:17.270
She couldn't have fallen from that height 
and escaped on her own power.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.620
Now, let's get to it.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.720
Action Field, on.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:35.790
Field Spell Crossover Acceleration!

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.750
Duel mode, on.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.170
Autopilot, stand by.

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:50.850
Riding duel...

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.440
Acceleration!

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:54.980
Duel!

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.290
I need to end this quickly!

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:06.760
I won't let you take the first turn.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:14.270
Now, Commons!

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:16.300
It's the beginning of our duel!

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:22.970
The first out of the Duel Palace, 
taking the first turn, is Shinji!

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:28.080
Remember the rage you felt when 
you watched my duel!

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.450
Remember our rage against the Tops!

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.650
This time, you must rise up!

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:38.890
Hey, I keep telling you to stop 
provoking the audience...

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.630
I understand your anger.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:45.860
That anger can overturn society.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:48.270
I'll lead you there!

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:51.800
So rise up, alongside me!

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:54.030
My turn!

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:57.280
I summon Battlewasp — Pin the Bullseye.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.710
Shinji summons a monster.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:05.420
But its attack points are a mere 200!

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:08.960
He talks big, but that isn't much at all.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.390
What can a monster like that do?

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:14.650
True, the monster I summoned is weak,

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:17.100
with only 200 attack points...

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:20.800
A monster as powerless as we, the Commons.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:25.000
But we fight with these powerless monsters.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.970
We've fought our way through this rotten society!

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:32.480
If these powerless monsters work together, 
they can overturn society.

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:34.680
That's what I'll show you!

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.620
I activate my monster's effect!

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:44.410
Once per turn, Pin the Bullseye can deal 
200 points of damage to my opponent.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:51.860
I set one card and end my turn.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:56.330
Shinji deals effect damage on the first turn!

00:10:56.600 --> 00:11:00.810
But he only has one 200-attack-point 
monster on the field.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:03.940
Even if I have only one monster on the field,

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:08.280
thousands and thousands of 
Commons are behind me.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:12.250
For their sakes, I must see 
this revolution succeed!

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:17.920
One 200-attack-point monster on the field.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:19.620
My turn!

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.590
I set the Pendulum Scale

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:27.420
with Scale 2 Performapal Gongato and 
Scale 6 Performapal Extra Slinger!

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:40.510
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 3 and 5 simultaneously!

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:43.510
Swing, my soul's pendulum.

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:46.520
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:48.040
Pendulum Summon!

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.510
Come out, my monsters!

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.690
Performapal Silver Claw.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.920
Performapal Salutiger.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:01.630
Yuya's executed his Pendulum Summon!

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:05.870
I activate my spell card Gap Power in my hand!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.430
When you have more life points than I do,

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:12.240
I increase the attack points of one of 
my monsters by half the difference!

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:13.340
What?

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.880
The difference between Shinji's 
life points and mine is 200.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.850
I increase Silver Claw's attack 
points by half of that, 100!

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:27.230
You used a spell card to increase 
its attack points by a mere 100?

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.700
Silver Claw attacks Pin the Bullseye!

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:36.520
The instant I declare battle, Silver Claw's 
effect increases the attack points

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.170
of all Performapals by 300 until the end of my turn!

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:43.480
The total attack points of my monsters 
are now 4200 altogether.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.140
I can finish you off with two straight attacks!

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:49.110
Yuya Sakaki is after a turn-one kill!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.250
So that's it...

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.350
Now, we can be done with that annoying Shinji.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:55.320
Shinji, don't lose!

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.370
Go, Silver Claw!

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:02.860
I activate my Continuous Trap Battlewasp 
— Nest, targeting Pin the Bullseye!

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.440
When the target monster is attacked,

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:12.040
I can Special Summon one monster, with the 
same name, from my hand or my deck,

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.240
and force an end to the Battle Phase!

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.140
Force an end to the Battle Phase?

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:21.110
But this effect can only be used twice, 
before the card is destroyed.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:28.920
Shinji not only blocked his opponent's attack,

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:32.020
but managed to summon a second monster!

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:33.990
Looking good, Shinji!

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:40.680
When the Battle Phase is over, 
Silver Claw's effect ends

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.440
and its attack points return to normal.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.180
Too bad.

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:49.770
Did you really think I would leave my 
monsters on the field undefended?

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:54.480
But he still has only two monsters 
with 200 attack points.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.760
On my next turn...

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:58.720
I end my turn!

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.900
He's distracted.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.060
He must be worried about Yuzu.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.530
My turn!

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:13.910
I summon Tuner Monster Battlewasp 
— Sting the Poison.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.290
And by negating this card's effect,

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.210
I can Special Summon it from my hand.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:25.370
Come out, Battlewasp — Twinbow the Attacker!

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:31.380
Level 2 Sting the Poison tunes 
Level 3 Twinbow the Attacker!

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:37.360
Furiously stinging needle, become a bow 
that can strike even heaven in a flash!

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:38.820
Synchro Summon!

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:43.360
Appear, Battlewasp — Azusa the Ghost Bow!

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:48.930
Shinji just completed a Synchro Summon!

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:50.770
2200 attack points?

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:53.740
Now, the signal rocket of revolution has launched!

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.840
Rise up, Commons...

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:57.580
Alongside me!

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:00.540
For the sake of the Commons' future!

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.770
Go, Shinji!

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.390
We're with you!

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.400
Will this be all right?

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:20.820
Yuya...

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.550
Now, will Shinji seize control of the duel

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:30.370
and turn things around, with his 
summoned Synchro Monster?!

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:36.700
Over there?

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:43.960
Rise up, Commons! Alongside me!

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:47.400
Hit them with the anger of the Commons,

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:49.890
who have been oppressed and 
trampled by the Tops!

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:52.410
I activate Azusa the Ghost Bow's effect.

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:56.080
It doubles the effect damage of 
one of its ally Battlewasps.

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.370
Double the damage?!

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:01.870
Now, Pin the Bullseye deals 400 damage.

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.840
I activate Pin the Bullseye's monster effect.

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:08.140
The Tops steal our homes,

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:11.080
daily leaving us to tremble with cold. 
This is our suffering!

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:23.240
They steal our food, leaving us 
starving. This is our rage!

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:31.530
This is the anger we feel toward the Tops

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.540
for the pain they've inflicted on us!

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:36.740
Azusa the Ghost Bow attacks Salutiger.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:51.560
Shinji's series of attacks has dealt 1300 damage!

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:53.470
Looking good, Shinji!

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.530
Crush him now!

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:04.500
Damn... What am I doing?

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:07.470
I can't save Yuzu like this.

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:10.330
Now, the revolution begins!

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.210
I'll use this card to overturn society.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.960
By sending Battlewasp — Dart the Hunter 
from my hand to the graveyard,

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:21.120
I deal effect damage to you, equal to the attack 
points of one monster in my graveyard.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:22.190
What?

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:27.430
And that effect damage is doubled 
by Azusa the Ghost Bow.

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:30.900
The attack points of Salutiger, just destroyed 
in the graveyard, are 1700.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:35.630
I deal double them, to 3400 
damage, and finish you!

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:54.790
Yuya!

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:01.770
Sora?

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:15.210
Just now, was that Sora?

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:26.620
But what's Sora doing there?

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:31.690
Sora?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.160
That's Yuzu's...

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.900
Yuzu... Yuzu's okay?

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:49.450
It's over.

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:54.080
I send Battlewasp — Dart the Hunter to 
the graveyard, to activate its effect!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:01.120
Sora... I believe in you!

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:11.230
Is it over?

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:21.000
I use Action Spell Acceleration 
to negate effect damage!

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:21.840
What?

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:25.280
Yuya makes it through!

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:32.180
Saved by the Action Card?

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.630
But you won't be so lucky next time.

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:38.500
Next turn, I'll defeat you and start my revolution!

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:39.520
I end my turn!

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.540
Watch me, Yuzu...

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:46.540
Just as Yuzu used her duel to warn 
people of the interdimensional war,

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:49.000
I'll use mine to keep winning.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:54.440
I'll win the Friendship Cup, and bring 
smiles to everyone in City!

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:59.170
Then I'll end the interdimensional war, 
and return home to everyone.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:03.980
To the principal, Futoshi, 
Ayu, Tatsuya, and Mom!

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:07.180
My turn!

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:15.900
I Pendulum Summon with the scale already set!

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:20.540
Come out, Timebreaker Magician.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.660
Yuya just Pendulum Summoned!

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.010
But he only summoned one monster.

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:31.210
Timebreaker Magician's monster effect activates!

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.840
When this card is the only one Pendulum 
Summoned from my hand,

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.740
its attack points double!

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:39.450
2800 attack points?

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:43.150
I attack Azusa the Ghost Bow 
with Timebreaker Magician!

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:54.470
And I attack Pin the Bullseye with Silver Claw.

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:56.480
The moment I declare battle,

00:20:56.480 --> 00:21:00.440
Silver Claw's attack points increase by 
300 until the Battle Phase's end!

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.100
I activate Battlewasp — Nest's effect.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.610
When Pin the Bullseye is attacked,

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:11.940
I Special Summon another Pin the Bullseye 
from my deck and end the Battle Phase.

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.770
Shinji prevents the second attack!

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:22.100
But the second use of Battlewasp — 
Nest causes it to be destroyed!

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:26.730
Now, you can't force an end 
to the Battle Phase again.

00:21:26.730 --> 00:21:28.160
I end my turn.

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:30.670
The real match starts now!

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:33.140
Yuya's dueling style has changed...

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:43.990
Getting serious now? But it's too late.

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:45.920
I'm not alone.

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:50.890
I have the will of thousands and thousands 
of Commons behind me.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:53.480
The revolution has already started!

00:21:53.860 --> 00:21:56.920
No one can stop us now!

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:04.540
It's my turn!

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:05.540
I won't lose.

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:08.010
I swore I'd win...

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.240
With my way of dueling!

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:53.290
I summon Tuning Magician!

00:23:53.290 --> 00:23:56.910
Yuya just made a clear mistake!

00:23:56.910 --> 00:24:00.950
He's summoned a Level 1 monster, 
with 0 defense points!

00:24:00.950 --> 00:24:02.670
Looks like it's over...

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:05.770
Your luck ended the moment you put 
that worthless card in your deck.

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:06.990
That isn't true!

00:24:06.990 --> 00:24:09.530
Every card has a purpose!

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:14.470
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Awakening Paladin.

00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:17.130
The fun is only getting started!
